  "numerical_failure": {
    "category": "special_value",
    "affected_api": "astropy.io.fits.CompImageHDU",
    "observed_behavior": "Compressing (u)int64 data into a compressed FITS image (CompImageHDU, e.g. via quantize_level/quantize_method=1 with RICE_1 or HCOMPRESS) produces a file where BYTEPIX is not set correctly (should be 8 for int64 data), and funpack of the resulting file is broken because of an upstream bug in HCOMPRESS for 64-bit ints.",
    "expected_behavior": "Compressing (u)int64 data should not silently create a broken compressed file: data should be converted to (u)int32 if possible without overflow, otherwise an error should be raised; HCOMPRESS should be disabled for 64-bit ints while GZIP algorithms keep working; BYTEPIX should be 8 for int64 data.",
    "manifestation": "wrong_value",
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "Writing int64 (or uint64) image data to a compressed FITS HDU (CompImageHDU / pack function in the reproducer)",
      "Compression algorithm RICE_1 or HCOMPRESS applied to 64-bit integer data",
      "quantize_level and quantize_method=1 set in the reproducer for the compressed HDU"
    ],
    "input_output_examples": [
      {
        "input": "data_hdu = fits.PrimaryHDU(data=np.random.poisson(1000, size=(ny, nx)), header=data_header) with nx, ny = 512, 517, packed via pack() into a CompImageHDU and written with writeto('test-fpack.fits.fz')",
        "buggy_output": "BYTEPIX not set to 8 (exact buggy value not stated in passages); funpack then fails or produces a broken result",
        "expected_output": "BYTEPIX should be 8 for int64 data; otherwise data converted to int32 without overflow or an error raised",
        "value_kind": "integer",
        "source": "issue#19577 reproducer and comment"
      }
    ],
    "oracle_clues": [
      "Comment states BYTEPIX should be 8 for int64 data",
      "Fix converts (u)int64 to (u)int32 if possible without overflow, otherwise raises an error",
      "Maintainer note: HCOMPRESS for 64-bit ints is broken upstream so it should be disabled; GZIP algorithms should keep working",
      "Added test test_decompress_integers expects ValueError on overflow or AstropyUserWarning otherwise for RICE_1 and PLIO_1 with 8-byte ints, matching 'compression doesn't support 64 integers'"
    ]
  },
  "numerical_characteristics": {
    "dtype": "(u)int64",
    "precision": null,
    "magnitude": null,
    "tolerance": null,
    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "The bug concerns creating FITS tile-compressed files from (u)int64 data; the fix converts data to (u)int32 when possible without overflow and otherwise raises an error.",
      "HCOMPRESS only supports 32-bit data per PR discussion; the '64' function is needed to avoid overflow for 32-bit ints, and 64-bit ints would need a '128' function in principle.",
      "The reproducer in issue#19577 packs a Poisson-distributed int image (np.random.poisson(1000)) with quantize_level 64 or 1e9 and quantize_method=1 and then runs funpack.",
      "The added test test_decompress_integers parametrizes nbytes in (2, 4, 8) and an overflow flag, adding np.iinfo(np.int32).max to the data to trigger overflow; for RICE_1 and PLIO_1 with 8-byte ints it expects ValueError on overflow or AstropyUserWarning otherwise, matching 'compression doesn't support 64 integers'.",
      "The changelog states RICE_1 or PLIO_1 compressed files with (u)int64 data are prevented; the commit notes some methods actually support 64-bit data.",
      "No passage describes NaN, infinity, signed zero, or subnormal handling; the special-value aspect is only about integer overflow at the int32 boundary."
    ],
    "reproduction_risks": [
      "The overflow case depends on adding int32 max to the data, which can wrap for int64 unless computed carefully; exact overflow behavior is not stated in passages.",
      "Behavior for methods other than RICE_1 and PLIO_1 with 64-bit data is only hinted at ('some methods actually support 64-bit data') and not specified."
    ]
  },
